{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792591679,"nonce":"wZFPW7sQHxPNPFiRvqfWSnzxrdE=","title":"LLVM: initialize native target registration once across threads","message":"The native-only llvm-sys target wrappers call LLVMInitialize* on every backend/MCJIT construction. Parallel LLVM-backed tests can register the host target more than once, after which Target::from_triple fails with \"Cannot choose between targets aarch64 and aarch64\". Reproduced by cargo test -p zyntax_compiler --features llvm-backend --lib --tests: all four bounded_div integration cases failed during concurrent LLVMJitBackend::new calls.\n\nUse one synchronized host-initialization guard shared by native and All target wrappers, including execution engines that call the exported C symbols directly. Preserve native-only linking. Cover simultaneous first initialization in a separate test process and repeat target lookup/backend creation across threads.","files":null}]}